                "snippet": "Prior Authorization Policy\n3. Services that require prior authorization\nThe decision turnaround is counted in business days from the time the payer receives a complete request. An expedited request is for a patient whose health or ability to regain function would be put at serious risk by the standard wait; the ordering provider must attest to this on the request. Service category\nAdvanced imaging, Examples = MRI, CT, PET scans, cardiac MRI. Advanced imaging, Prior authorization = Required. Advanced imaging, Standard decision = 5 business days. Advanced imaging, Expedited decision = 24 hours. Advanced imaging, Submit at least = 5 business days before the scan. Elective inpatient admission, Examples = Planned surgery, scheduled medical admission. Elective inpatient admission, Prior authorization = Required. Elective inpatient admission, Standard decision = 3 business days. Elective inpatient admission, Expedited decision = 24 hours. Elective inpatient admission, Submit at least = 7 business days before admission. Outpatient surgery, Examples = Ambulatory surgery and endoscopic procedures. Outpatient surgery, Prior authorization = Required. Outpatient surgery, Standard decision = 5 business days. Outpatient surgery, Expedited decision = 48 hours. Outpatient surgery, Submit at least = 7 business days before the procedure. Cardiac rehabilitation, Examples = Phase II supervised exercise program. Cardiac rehabilitation, Prior authorization = Required. Cardiac rehabilitation, Standa",
