                "publishedAt": null,
                "snippet": "Prior Authorization Policy\n4. How to request authorization\n- The ordering provider documents the clinical reason in the order. The order is not released to scheduling until the authorization status is \"approved\" or \"not required\".\n- The Utilization Management coordinator submits the request through the payer’s portal or by fax on the same day the order is signed, attaching the clinical notes the payer’s criteria require.\n- The coordinator records the reference number and the decision due date in the electronic record and checks the status daily until a decision arrives.\n- If the payer asks for more information, the coordinator returns it within 2 business days. The payer’s clock restarts when the information arrives.\n- If the request is denied, the ordering provider decides within 2 business days whether to appeal or to change the order. A peer-to-peer call is requested for every denial of an advanced imaging or elective inpatient request.",
