                "snippet": "Prior Authorization Policy\n4. How to request authorization\n6. When authorization is missing\nIf a service was delivered without a required authorization the coordinator asks the payer for a retrospective authorization within 14 days of the service. Where the service was an emergency, the emergency notification rule in section 3 applies and no authorization is needed. Claims that are denied for \"Prior authorization missing\" are sent to Denials Management and are written off only after the appeal window in the payer’s contract has closed.\nSynthetic document for demonstration only. Riverside Health Network is fictional. Page 2 of 3\nRIVERSIDE HEALTH NETWORK RHN-REV-021 | Version 2.4",
